requirement_summery:
Collaborate with Business operations, Product, Algorithms, Strategies and engineering teams to build data solutions for critical business problems, and find new opportunities for growth;
Conduct insightful analysis to drive business impact. Analyze data for trends and patterns, and interpret data with clear objectives in mind;
Serve as lead data strategist to identify and integrate new datasets that can be leveraged through our product capabilities, and work closely with the engineering team in the development of data products;
Research and devise innovative statistical models, analytical experiments (A/B tests) for data analysis, and keep current with technical and industry developments;
Utilize algorithms and models to mine big-data stores; perform data and error analysis to improve models; clean and validate data for uniformity and accuracy;
Adopt AI in daily workstreams and building AI data solutions for automated and scalable analysis.
Bachelor degree or above, computer, statistics, mathematics and other related majors are preferred; English can be used as a working language;
Skilled in SQL, EXCEL, Python at least one scripting language, familiar with common data statistics and analysis methods;
Good communication skills, teamwork spirit and initiative;
Good logical thinking ability, business interpretation ability and fast learning ability;
Sensitive to numbers and passionate about data analysis.
Internship experience in Data Science/Data Analyst area.

